          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1145,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.125.330:block:1",
          "start": 767
        },
        "quote": "(b) Each retiree who elects to obtain or continue health care benefits coverage hereunder shall be required to contribute premium payments to the plan for the basic or extended coverage elected, including the administrative costs thereof, but such contribution shall not exceed the percentage of the premium cost for other similarly situated employees as specified by State law.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.125.330:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 2.125.330 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "9947ef38-aea2-5e56-b4a8-12d3d4cbc3c5",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1524,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.125.330:block:2",
          "start": 1146
        },
        "quote": "(c) Eligibility for coverage under the plan may cease to be made available upon (1) the retired employee reaching age 65 and/or becoming eligible for Medicare, (2) the retired employee failing to make required premium payments on a timely basis, or (3) the retired employee becoming covered under a health care benefits plan of another employer. (Ord. 20206 §§ 72, 86, 9-10-19.)",
